LAMMPS (10 Dec 2025)
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
# Reconstruct a data file from a native LAMMPS dump snapshot.
# A template data file supplies the existing box, masses and atom types.
#
# Usage:
# lmp -in in.dump2data \
#   -var template ../outputs/stage1_minimized.data \
#   -var dump ../outputs/stage2_anneal.dump \
#   -var timestep 20000 \
#   -var out ../outputs/rebuilt.data

units metal
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p

read_data ${template}
read_data outputs/stage1_minimized.data
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0.28932551 0 0) to (66.235885 33.262605 35.061865)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  3600 atoms
  reading velocities ...
  3600 velocities
  read_data CPU = 0.014 seconds

read_dump ${dump} ${timestep} x y z vx vy vz   box yes replace yes trim yes add keep format native
read_dump outputs/stage2_anneal.dump ${timestep} x y z vx vy vz   box yes replace yes trim yes add keep format native
read_dump outputs/stage2_anneal.dump 20000 x y z vx vy vz   box yes replace yes trim yes add keep format native
Adding 'type' field to requested per-atom fields
Scanning dump file ...
Reading snapshot from dump file ...
  orthogonal box = (0.28932551 0 0) to (66.235885 33.262605 35.061865)
  3600 atoms before read
  3600 atoms in snapshot
  0 atoms purged
  3600 atoms replaced
  0 atoms trimmed
  0 atoms added
  3600 atoms after read

write_data ${out}
write_data outputs/dump2data_validation/rebuilt_stage2.data
System init for write_data ...
WARNING: Communication cutoff is 0.0. No ghost atoms will be generated. Energies and forces may be wrong and atoms may get lost. (src/comm_brick.cpp:188)
print "DUMP2DATA_DONE"
DUMP2DATA_DONE
